data readable_witness_enrollment_note: String = "The six readability witnesses below (raw-text style serialization, chip min-width, container centering, the <details> disclosure, the dispatch accent) were authored with the fixes they verify but never bundled into this file's only `test fn`, and discovery keys on the `test fn `/`test data ` prefix — so they had ZERO executing consumers and CI was blind to the exact regressions they were written to catch. Proven by execution rather than by reading, 2026-07-24: reverting `.status` min-width back to width (the original defect) left roadmap_page_keystone_holds returning true. That is the orphaned-enrollment shape DESIGN calls coverage by illusion, and an inert witness is a lie about coverage, so they are enrolled here. Every witness in this file is now reachable from this one entry; adding an unbundled `fn witness_*` is the defect to look for in review."

// THE UPDATES NEGATIVE WAS A FACT ABOUT THE AUTHORITY'S CONTENT, NOT ABOUT THE RENDERER. When this
// row was written no authored ticket carried an update, so "the authority page holds no
// ticket-updates block" stood in for "a ticket with no updates renders no updates block". Tickets
// have since gained dated notes through gunbc.roadmap_authority updated, and the page legitimately
// renders them -- so the page-wide negative redded on correct output while saying nothing about the
// property. The property is the renderer's (disclosure_updates_block renders nothing for an empty
// thread and one block for a non-empty one), so it is asserted over two supplied tickets differing
// ONLY in their updates, in both directions; the row's structure is asserted over a supplied ticket,
// and its real-authority inhabitance lives in witness_real_ticket_row_renders_structured.
fn updates_fixture(updates: List<gunbc.roadmap_status.TicketUpdate>) -> RoadmapNode {
  fx_ticket_row(identity: "rnfx_UPD8TESFXTR3KZ0MQ7WV", id: "updates-fixture", done: false, t: TicketFields {
    headline: "fixture",
    brief: "a brief",
    displaced_cost: "",
    current_state: "",
    first_slice: "",
    red_control: "",
    out_of_scope: "",
    handback: "",
    updates: updates,
    authored_on: "",
    last_verified_on: "",
  })
}

// ONE ROW, NOT ONE PAGE. The ticket-row claims below ask what the ROW renderer emits for a row of a
// given kind, so they supply the row and serialize it through nodes_ul -- the same route
// witness_bold_title_renders_strong takes -- rather than paying for the whole authority page once per
// claim (DESIGN section 3, a witness discriminates at one interface). The pairing obligation is held by
// witness_authority_serializes_with_structure, which asserts that the REAL authority page emits a
// ticket-row "inspect" disclosure, a ticket brief, a disclosure field and a carrier link: the route
// these fixtures supply is still executed for real -- by witness_real_ticket_row_renders_structured,
// which takes an AUTHORED ticket from gunbc.roadmap_authority declared_roadmap_nodes through the same
// row route, so real authored data reaches the real renderer without paying for the whole page.
fn row_html(rn: RoadmapNode) -> HtmlEmitResult {
  try_serialize_html_source(node: nodes_ul(items: [rn], nodes: [rn], edges: [], merged: [], fuel: 0,
    launch: gunbc.roadmap_page.page_launch_context(doc: launch_fixture_doc(nodes: [rn], edges: []), merged: [], launch: dispatch_doc_standing())))
}

fn is_real_structured_ticket(rn: RoadmapNode) -> Bool {
  match line_ticket(item: rn.line) {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: t } => t.displaced_cost != "" && count(rn.carriers) > 0
  }
}

// THE INHABITANCE CLAIM FOR THE SUPPLIED TICKET ROWS (DESIGN section 3 pairing). It selects the first
// authored ticket carrying a displaced cost and a carrier rather than naming one, so it follows the
// authority as tickets are accepted; an authority with no such ticket reds here, by name.
test fn witness_real_ticket_row_renders_structured() -> Bool {
  match filter(declared_roadmap_nodes(), rn => is_real_structured_ticket(rn: rn)).first() {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: rn } =>
      match row_html(rn: rn) {
        EmitRejected { reason: _ } => false
        EmitOk { html: h } =>
          string_contains(s: h, pattern: "<details class=\"taskbar-inspect\"><summary>inspect</summary>")
            && string_contains(s: h, pattern: "class=\"ticket-brief\"")
            && string_contains(s: h, pattern: ">displaced cost</span>")
            && string_contains(s: h, pattern: "href=\"https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/main/")
      }
  }
}

