data combinator_witness_repoint_note: String = "Repointed at A1: the former subject '.node-superseded > .title' was an UNREACHABLE selector — direct-child, while .title actually nests two levels down (.node-head > .node-mid > .title), so the strikethrough could never paint; the rule now uses the descendant combinator and the escape-guard witness repoints to a selector that still legitimately carries '>' (the section-fold summary). The claim under test is unchanged: a raw '>' inside emitted style text must not be entity-escaped."

// THE STYLE ELEMENT'S TEXT THROUGH THE REAL PAGE SERIALIZER, over the real rule blocks: a page with
// one row whose head carries the serialized rules (the stylesheet seam
// roadmap_page_launch_with_stylesheet), so a claim about how the page emits rule text reads the
// emitted page without deriving the audition and root blocks no such claim reads. The rule text
// itself is the real one; the sheet-wide absences ride fx_css_part_holds.
